 The analyses also followed different targets. Phenolic recovery used a Folin–Ciocalteau measurement calibrated with gallic acid, alongside phenolic-acid chromatography. Pectin characterization examined sugar composition, molecular-size distribution and methylation, among other properties. Extraction conditions changed the pectin populations recovered. [3, §§2.3, 3.3–3.5]
 
-This study provides a useful sourcing distinction: **“made from apple pomace” describes a starting material, not the identity of the resulting ingredient**. Request which fraction is collected, which soluble or insoluble material is removed, and what remains in the powder. A phenolic extract should not inherit the water-binding specification of the residual fibre; a pectin ingredient should not inherit the phenolic assay of the first extraction stream.
+This study provides a useful sourcing distinction: **“made from apple pomace” describes a starting material, not the identity of the resulting ingredient**. Ask which fraction is collected, which soluble or insoluble components are removed, and what remains in the powder. A phenolic extract should not inherit the water-binding specification of the residual fibre; a pectin ingredient should not inherit the phenolic assay of the first extraction stream.
 
 The paper's laboratory radical-scavenging test is likewise not a finished-food shelf-life test. If an extract is being considered to control oxidation in a formula, compare it against the appropriate control in that food, using its actual processing and storage conditions. That is a separate development question from measuring the incoming extract's phenolic content.
 
